Z||000004||ChadMan||10-20-2000||12:47 PM||||The museum is in Clinton, OK, west of OK City about halfway to the TX border.  <A HREF="http://www.route66.org" TARGET=_blank>www.route66.org</A> <P>The silver 86 SE belongs to my in-laws.  They left it with us in 3/99 when they moved to Phoenix and we delivered it to them three months later.  It's a great-running car - 70K miles, automatic, working air, PW, PDL, tilt, cruise, factory subwoofer.  He offered it to me for $2800, then changed his mind.<P>I wouldn't mind having it, but I don't really lust after it because it has an automatic and no sunroof, and it has been hit in the rear and repaired a while back (note the non-factory location of the wing - it's about six inches forward on the rear deck from where it should be).  The paint is pretty good though.||||reg||1
